<%#
  The Voice Packs card (#1145): installed voice packs (#1034) and the ones
  downloadable from iRaceDeck's own catalog (#1100). Was the tail of
  race-engineer-settings.ejs; a card of its own since #1145 so the lists get the
  card's full width and every voice-pack control sits in one place.

  Settings-window only: every command below (voicePackRefresh /
  voicePackInstall / voicePackRemove / openVoicePacksFolder) is handled by the
  settings-window command handler, and a Property Inspector's `sendToPlugin`
  goes to its own action instead — the same reason `ird-open-folder` is gated
  in global-common-diagnostics.ejs. The window passes the flag to THIS include
  explicitly (see voice-packs-partial.test.ts for why).
%>
<% if (locals.settingsWindow) { %>
<%- include('section-header', { title: 'Installed Voices' }) %>
<ird-voice-pack-list packs="_voicePacks"></ird-voice-pack-list>
<div class="ird-supporting-text ird-supporting-text-full">
  Voice packs live in <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\iRaceDeck\Race Engineer\Voices</code> and survive plugin updates.
  Add a pack folder there, then rescan. A pack that cannot be loaded is listed with the reason. A pack you no
  longer want can be removed here too.
</div>
<div class="ird-open-settings">
  <ird-voice-pack-refresh></ird-voice-pack-refresh>
  <ird-open-voice-packs-folder></ird-open-voice-packs-folder>
</div>
<%- include('section-header', { title: 'Available to Download' }) %>
<ird-voice-pack-catalog status="_voicePackStatus"></ird-voice-pack-catalog>
<div class="ird-supporting-text ird-supporting-text-full">
  Packs iRaceDeck publishes itself. Press Install (or Update, once a newer version is out) and iRaceDeck
  downloads, verifies and installs it for you — this can happen while iRacing is running.
</div>
<% } %>
